\ UNARC                                             RS 12/20/87                                                                 \   The following Source Code will provide you with the         \   ability to extract most files from archives created         \   with the MS-DOS programs, ARC_5.1 and PKARC.                \   Both of these programs use various methods of file          \   compression - UNARC is not currently capable of             \   extracting some of these types.  For the most part,         \   the unsupported types are OLD methods that are              \   supported by ARC and PKARC only to maintain backwards       \   compatibility with earlier versions of themselves.          \                                                               \   The two operative words are :                               \                                                               \   ARCList -   lists all the files in an archive               \   UNARC   -   extracts files from an archive                  \ UNARC - load screen                               RS 12/21/87                                                                 \   written by                                                  \   R. W. Shepard                                               \   P.O. Box 1344                                               \   Kodiak, Alaska  99615                                       \   (907) 486-4076                                              \                                                                                                                                                                                                       2   LOAD    \ setup for array sizes and max compression                     \ type code.                                                                                                    3  40   THRU    \ just load 'the rest'                                                                                                                                                      \ UNARC - setup memory usage, archive types         RS 12/21/87                                                                 \   If you will NOT NEED to extract files from PKARC archives   \   or you DO NOT have at least 30k of FREE DICTIONARY SPACE -  \   'comment out' the following two lines.                                                                                          13 CONSTANT Max_Bits    \ max bits/code - PKARC files           10 CONSTANT Max_Type    \ max type we can handle + 1                                                                        \   OTHERWISE - 'comment out' these two lines.                                                                                  \   12 CONSTANT Max_Bits    \ max bits/code - ARC files         \    9 CONSTANT Max_Type    \ max type we can handle + 1                                                                        \   MAKE SURE that you set the CONSTANT, Sect_Size, on Screen   \   9 to reflect reality on your system. Also - LOOK AT Scr 15  \ Preamble                                          RS 12/15/87                                                                 : SHIFT             \ u1 n --- u2                                                                                                   ?DUP                                                            IF   DUP ABS 0 ROT 0<                                                IF   DO 2/ 32767 AND LOOP                                       ELSE DO 2*           LOOP                                       THEN                                                       THEN ;                                                                                                                      : D+!               \ d addr ---                                                                                                    DUP >R 2@ D+ R> 2! ;                                                                                                                                                                        \ Preamble                                          RS 12/15/87                                                                 : ?SYSERR           \ erc ---                                                                                                       ?DUP                                                            IF   CR CR ." File error # " U. CR QUIT                         THEN ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \ UNARC - constants                                 RS 12/21/87                                                                 144              CONSTANT DLE_Char      \ marks RL string       256              CONSTANT HUF_EOF       \ EOF mark - Huffman    257              CONSTANT Num_Nodes     \ # Huffman nodes       Num_Nodes NEGATE CONSTANT Empty_Mark    \ empty node marker     256              CONSTANT Clear_Code    \ 're-init' code - LZW  257              CONSTANT First_Free    \ first code to use     9                CONSTANT Init_Bits     \ initial bits/code                                                                                                                                     1 Max_Bits SHIFT CONSTANT Abs_Max_Code  \ abs max code val      Abs_Max_Code     CONSTANT Suffix_Size   \ size of suffix array  Abs_Max_Code 2*  CONSTANT Prefix_Size   \ size of prefix array                                                                                                                                  \ UNARC - variables, arrays                         RS 12/20/87                                                                 VARIABLE Free_Code           \ next code to use                 VARIABLE Max_Code            \ max code for current nbits       VARIABLE nBits               \ number of bits in current code   VARIABLE Input_Code          \ last code read                   VARIABLE fClear              \ flag - true = 're-init' received                                                                                                                                 CREATE (prefix)         Prefix_Size ALLOT   \ array for codes                                                                   \ the Prefix array will also be used to store the Huffman       \ tree when expanding a squeezed file                                                                                           CREATE (suffix)         Suffix_Size ALLOT   \ array for chars                                                                   \ UNARC - array words                               RS 12/16/87                                                                 : Prefix            \ index --- addr    | entry in codes array                                                                      2* (prefix) + ;                                                                                                             : Suffix            \ index --- addr    | entry in chars array                                                                      (suffix) + ;                                                                                                                                                                                : Set_Max_Code      \ ---       | sets max code val for nbits                                                                       1 nBits @ SHIFT 1- Max_Code ! ;                                                                                                                                                             \ UNARC - array words                               RS 12/20/87                                                                 : Left_Node         \ index --- addr    | left node in HUF tree                                                                     2* 2* (prefix) + ;                                                                                                          : Right_Node        \ index --- addr    | right node in HUF tree                                                                    Left_Node 2+ ;                                                                                                              : HUF_Tree          \ index bit --- addr    | 0 = left  branch                      \                       | 1 = right branch                                                                      2* SWAP Left_Node + ;                                                                                                                                                                       \ UNARC - File I/O - bytes                          RS 12/20/87                                                                 FCB In_File                         \ input file control block                                                                  512             CONSTANT Sect_Size  \ bytes/sector              Sect_Size 1-    CONSTANT Size_Mask  \ bytes/sector mask                                                                                                                                         CREATE In_Buf   Sect_Size ALLOT     \ input file buffer                                                                                                                                         VARIABLE iInput_Buf  \ index to current byte in input buffer    VARIABLE Bytes_Left  \ unread bytes in last sector              VARIABLE fLast_Sect  \ true if processing last sector                                                                                                                                           \ UNARC - File I/O - bytes                          RS 12/16/87                                                                 : Open_Input        \ --- erc                                                                                                       0 iInput_Buf ! 0 Bytes_Left ! FALSE fLast_Sect !                In_File OPEN ;                                                                                                              : Close_Input       \ ---                                                                                                           In_File CLOSE ;                                                                                                             : Read_Sect         \ ---                                                                                                           In_File In_Buf SREAD DUP 0> fLast_Sect !                        Sect_Size SWAP - Bytes_Left ! 0 iInput_Buf ! ;                                                                              \ UNARC - File I/O - bytes                          RS 12/16/87                                                                 2VARIABLE Bytes_Read                    \ counts bytes read                                                                     : Read_Byte         \ --- byte flag     | false = ok                                                                                Bytes_Left @ 0= fLast_Sect @ NOT AND                            IF   Read_Sect                                                  THEN In_Buf iInput_Buf @ + C@                                   -1 Bytes_Left +! 1 iInput_Buf +! 1 0 Bytes_Read D+!             Bytes_Left @ 0< ;                                                                                                           : Get_Byte          \ --- byte          | null if no byte avail                                                                     Read_Byte ABORT" Read_Byte FAILED - File Error" ;                                                                           \ UNARC - File I/O - bytes                          RS 12/16/87                                                                 FCB Out_File                        \ output file control block                                                                 CREATE Out_Buf  Sect_Size ALLOT     \ output file buffer                                                                        VARIABLE iOut_Buf       \ index to curr. byte in output buffer  VARIABLE fOverwriting   \ flag - true if overwriting a file     VARIABLE fOvw_Ok        \ flag - true if overwrite is ok                                                                        : Check_Overwrite   \ --- flag      | true = overwrite ok                                                                           CR Out_File .FCB SPACE ." already exists, overwrite (y/n) "     KEY 32 OR ASCII y = DUP fOvw_Ok ! ;                                                                                                                                                         \ UNARC - File I/O - bytes                          RS 12/16/87                                                                 : Create_Output     \ --- flag          | true = all ok                                                                             Out_File OPEN 0= DUP fOverwriting !                             IF   Check_Overwrite 0=                                              IF   Out_File CLOSE FALSE EXIT                                  THEN Out_File DELETE ?SYSERR                               THEN 0 iOut_Buf ! Out_Buf Sect_Size 26 FILL                     Out_File MAKEFILE ?SYSERR TRUE ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            \ UNARC - File I/O - bytes                          RS 12/16/87                                                                 : Write_Sect        \ ---           | writes the output buffer                                                                      Out_File Out_Buf SWRITE                                         ABORT" Unable to WRITE output buffer "                          Out_Buf Sect_Size 26 FILL ;                                                                                                 : Write_Byte        \ byte ---      | writes a byte to Out_File                                                                     Out_Buf iOut_Buf @ + C!                                         iOut_Buf @ 1+ Size_Mask AND                                     DUP iOut_Buf ! 0=                                               IF   Write_Sect                                                 THEN ;                                                                                                                      \ UNARC - File I/O - bytes                          RS 12/16/87                                                                 : Close_Output      \ ---               | closes Out_File                                                                           iOut_Buf @ 0>                                                   IF   iOut_Buf @ Out_File 10 + !     \ * sets last sect size          Write_Sect                                                 THEN Out_File CLOSE ;                                                                                                                                                                       \ * This allows us to write the last sector of the file at      \   some size smaller than a disk sector.  It is virtually      \   guaranteed that you MUST either CHANGE this line or         \   REMOVE it entirely for proper operation with your FORTH.    \   In any event - the sector buffer is padded with ^Z's.                                                                       \ UNARC - File I/O - bits                           RS 12/16/87                                                                 VARIABLE Input_Byte             \ bit buffer                    VARIABLE Bits_Left              \ # valid bits left in buffer                                                                   : Start_Bits_In     \ ---       | setup to input bits                                                                               0 Bits_Left ! ;                                                                                                             : Input_Bit         \ --- bit   | read one bit from the file                                                                        Bits_Left @ 0=                                                  IF   Read_Byte 0= AND Input_Byte ! 8 Bits_Left !                THEN Input_Byte @ DUP -1 SHIFT Input_Byte ! 1 AND               -1 Bits_Left +! ;                                                                                                           \ UNARC - ARC header specific code                  RS 12/20/87                                                                 VARIABLE ARC_iBuf   \ 'fake' index into ARC's bit buffer        VARIABLE ARC_sBuf   \ 'fake' size of ARC's bit buffer                                                                           \ these variables allow us to stay 'aligned' with the input file\ in the same manner that ARC would - CRITICAL at Re_Init time                                                                  : Read_Code         \ --- code                                                                                                      ARC_iBuf @ ARC_sBuf @ < NOT                                     IF   0 ARC_iBuf ! nBits @ DUP 3 SHIFT SWAP 1- - ARC_sBuf !      THEN nBits @ ARC_iBuf +! 0 nBits @ 0                            DO   -1 SHIFT Input_Bit 0<> 32768 AND OR                        LOOP nBits @ 16 - SHIFT ;                                                                                                   \ UNARC - ARC header specific code                  RS 12/20/87                                                                 CREATE ARC_Hdr      30 ALLOT                                                                                                    ARC_Hdr      CONSTANT Hdr_Mark      \ header mark - always 26   ARC_Hdr 01 + CONSTANT ARC_Type      \ compression type          ARC_Hdr 02 + CONSTANT File_Name     \ filename - null terminate ARC_Hdr 15 + CONSTANT sComp_Data    \ DW - compressed size      ARC_Hdr 19 + CONSTANT File_Date     \ MSDOS date stamp          ARC_Hdr 21 + CONSTANT File_Time     \ MSDOS time stamp          ARC_Hdr 23 + CONSTANT Data_CRC      \ CRC of original file      ARC_Hdr 25 + CONSTANT sOrig_File    \ DW - size of orig file    ARC_Hdr 29 + CONSTANT ARC_Bits      \ max bits/code - type 8                                                                    CREATE ARCed_Name   14 ALLOT        \ filename as counted string                                                                \ UNARC - ARC header specific code                  RS 12/20/87                                                                 : Pack_Name         \ ---       | cnv name to cnt'd string                                                                          File_Name 13 0                                                  DO   DUP I + C@ 0=                                                   IF   I LEAVE                                                    THEN                                                       LOOP ARCed_Name 2DUP C! 1+ SWAP CMOVE ;                                                                                     : Check_ARC_Hdr     \ --- comp_type     |   0 = bad_header                                                                          sComp_Data 2@ SWAP sComp_Data 2!    \ DW to FORTH dbl num       sOrig_File 2@ SWAP sOrig_File 2!    \ DW to FORTH dbl num       ARC_Type C@ Hdr_Mark C@ 26 = AND ;                                                                                          \ UNARC - ARC header specific code                  RS 12/20/87                                                                 : Read_Hdr_Suffix   \ --- comp_type     |   0 = bad_header                                                                          29 2                                                            DO   Get_Byte ARC_Hdr I + C!                                    LOOP 0.0 Bytes_Read 2! Check_ARC_Hdr ;                                                                                      : Read_ARC_Hdr      \ --- comp_type     | -1 = bad header/EOF                                                                       Get_Byte DUP Hdr_Mark C! 26 =                                   IF   Get_Byte DUP ARC_Type C! 0<>                                    IF   Read_Hdr_Suffix Pack_Name EXIT                             THEN                                                       THEN -1 ;                                                                                                                   \ UNARC - Lempel-Zev decode                         RS 12/20/87                                                                 VARIABLE Cur_Code    \ current code value                       VARIABLE Old_Code    \ old code value                           VARIABLE Fin_Code    \ 'final' code value - decoded character   VARIABLE fDLE        \ flag - true = DLE received               VARIABLE nChars      \ # characters 'stacked' for output        VARIABLE Last_Char   \ last character output - used by RL code                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \ UNARC - Lempel-Zev decode                         RS 12/16/87                                                                 : Clear_Arrays      \ ---               | init the arrays                                                                           0 Prefix Prefix_Size -1 FILL                                    0 Suffix Suffix_Size -1 FILL ;                                                                                              : Reset_Input       \ ---               | skip garbage data                                                                         BEGIN  ARC_iBuf @ ARC_sBuf @ <                                  WHILE  Read_Code DROP                                           REPEAT ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \ UNARC - Lempel-Zev decode                         RS 12/16/87                                                                 : Get_Code          \ --- code                                                                                                      Free_Code @ Max_Code @ > nBits @ Max_Bits < AND                 IF   Reset_Input 1 nBits +! Set_Max_Code                             ARC_sBuf @ ARC_iBuf !                                      THEN fClear @                                                   IF   Init_Bits nBits ! Set_Max_Code fClear OFF                  THEN Read_Code ;                                                                                                            : Start_Decode      \ ---       | read first code & init vars                                                                       Get_Code DUP Input_Code ! DUP Last_Char ! DUP Cur_Code !        DUP Old_Code ! DUP Fin_Code ! Write_Byte ;                                                                                  \ UNARC - Lempel-Zev decode                         RS 12/16/87                                                                 : Unpack_Bytes      \ byte ---          | expand RL data                                                                            DUP 0=                              \ if 0 (cnt) - RL data      IF   2+ DLE_Char Last_Char !        \ is a single DLE char      THEN Last_Char @ SWAP 1- 0                                      DO   DUP Write_Byte                                             LOOP DROP fDLE OFF ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \ UNARC - Lempel-Zev decode                         RS 12/16/87                                                                 : Save_Byte(s)      \ byte ---          | write byte to output                                                                      fDLE @                                                          IF   Unpack_Bytes EXIT                                          THEN DUP DLE_Char =                                             IF   DROP fDLE ON EXIT                                          THEN DUP Last_Char ! Write_Byte ;                                                                                           : Pop_Chars         \ char(1) ... char(n) ---                                                                                       nChars @ 0                                                      ?DO  Save_Byte(s)                                               LOOP 0 nChars ! ;                                                                                                           \ UNARC - Lempel-Zev decode                         RS 12/16/87                                                                 : Decomp_Init       \ ---               | setup for LZW decomp                                                                      Init_Bits nBits ! Set_Max_Code                                  First_Free Free_Code !                                          fClear OFF fDLE OFF                                             0 ARC_sBuf ! 0 ARC_iBuf ! 0 nChars !                            Clear_Arrays 256 0                                              DO   0 I Prefix ! I DUP Suffix C!                               LOOP Start_Decode ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         \ UNARC - Lempel-Zev decode                         RS 12/16/87                                                                 : Re_Init           \ clear_code --- input_code                                                                                     DROP 256 0                                                      DO   0 I Prefix !                                               LOOP fClear ON                                                  Reset_Input First_Free 1- Free_Code !                           Get_Code DUP Input_Code ! ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \ UNARC - Lempel-Zev decode                         RS 12/16/87                                                                 : Decode            \ input_code --- char(1) ... char(n)                                                                            DUP Cur_Code ! DUP Free_Code @ < NOT                            IF   DROP Fin_Code @ 1 nChars +!                                     Old_Code @ DUP Cur_Code !                                  THEN                                                            BEGIN  DUP 255 >                                                WHILE  DUP Suffix C@ SWAP 1 nChars +!                                  Prefix @  DUP Cur_Code !                                 REPEAT Suffix C@ DUP Fin_Code !                                 Save_Byte(s) Pop_Chars ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \ UNARC - Lempel-Zev decode                         RS 12/21/87                                                                 : Add_Decomp_Code   \ ---               | add a code to the tbl                                                                     Free_Code @ Abs_Max_Code <                                      IF   Old_Code @ Free_Code @ Prefix !                                 Fin_Code @ Free_Code @ Suffix C!                                1 Free_Code +!                                             THEN Input_Code @ Old_Code ! ;                                                                                              : Skip_File         \ ---               | skip types 5,6,7                                                                          BEGIN  Bytes_Read 2@ sComp_Data 2@ D<                           WHILE  Get_Byte DROP                                            REPEAT ;                                                                                                                    \ UNARC - Unpack file                               RS 12/16/87                                                                 : UnPack_File       \ ---               | unpack types 1,2,3                                                                        fDLE OFF                                                        BEGIN  Bytes_Read 2@ sComp_Data 2@ D<                           WHILE  Get_Byte ARC_Type C@ 3 =                                        IF   Save_Byte(s)                                               ELSE Write_Byte                                                 THEN                                                     REPEAT ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \ UNARC - Huffman decode                            RS 12/20/87                                                                 VARIABLE HUF_Bits_Left      \ valid bits left in current code   VARIABLE HUF_Byte           \ current Huffman code                                                                              : Read_Integer      \ --- n         | reads integer from file                                                                       Get_Byte Get_Byte 8 SHIFT + ;                                                                                               : Get_HUF_Bit       \ --- bit       | get a bit from curr code                                                                      HUF_Bits_Left @ 0=                                              IF   Get_Byte DUP HUF_Byte ! 7 HUF_Bits_Left !                  ELSE HUF_Byte @ -1 SHIFT DUP HUF_Byte ! -1 HUF_Bits_Left +!     THEN 1 AND ;                                                                                                                \ UNARC - Huffman decode                            RS 12/20/87                                                                 : Read_HUF_Tree     \ ---       | read the Huffman tree                                                                             Empty_Mark 0 Left_Node ! Empty_Mark 0 Right_Node !              0 HUF_Bits_Left ! Read_Integer 0                                DO   Read_Integer I Left_Node  !                                     Read_Integer I Right_Node !                                LOOP ;                                                                                                                      : Decode_HUF_Byte      \ --- byte       | get a decoded byte                                                                        0 BEGIN  DUP 0< NOT                                               WHILE  Get_HUF_Bit HUF_Tree @                                   REPEAT 1+ NEGATE ;                                                                                                        \ UNARC - Huffman decode                            RS 12/21/87                                                                 : UnHUF_File        \ ---               | decode type 4                                                                             Read_HUF_Tree fDLE OFF                                          BEGIN  Bytes_Read 2@ sComp_Data 2@ D<                           WHILE  Decode_HUF_Byte DUP HUF_EOF <                                   IF   Save_Byte(s)                                               ELSE DROP                                                       THEN                                                     REPEAT ;                                                                                                                    : Get_ARC_Name      \ ---                                                                                                           CR ." Enter ARC File name : " QUERY In_File FILENAME ;                                                                      \ UNARC - Lempel-Zev decode                         RS 12/21/87                                                                 : UnCrunch_File     \ ---               | uncrunch type 8                                                                           ARC_Type C@ 8 =                                                 IF   Get_Byte DROP                                              THEN Start_Bits_In Decomp_Init                                  BEGIN  Bytes_Read 2@ sComp_Data 2@ D<                           WHILE  Get_Code DUP Input_Code ! DUP Clear_Code =                      IF   Re_Init                                                    THEN Decode Add_Decomp_Code                              REPEAT ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \ UNARC - extract, list words                       RS 12/20/87                                                                 : List_Header       \ ---                                                                                                           CR ." File            Type    Date       Time" 6 SPACES            ." OrigSize    CompSize" CR 65 0                             DO   ASCII - EMIT                                               LOOP CR ;                                                                                                                   : Two_Digits        \ n ---                                                                                                         ABS 0 <# # # #> TYPE ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \ UNARC - extract, list words                       RS 12/20/87                                                                 : .File_Time        \ ---                                                                                                           File_Time @ DUP 31 AND SWAP -5 SHIFT DUP 63 AND SWAP -6         SHIFT Two_Digits ASCII : EMIT Two_Digits ASCII : EMIT           2* Two_Digits ;                                                                                                             : .File_Date        \ ---                                                                                                           File_Date @ DUP 31 AND SWAP -5 SHIFT DUP 15 AND SWAP            -4 SHIFT 80 + ROT ROT Two_Digits ASCII - EMIT Two_Digits        ASCII - EMIT Two_Digits ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \ UNARC - extract, list words                       RS 12/20/87                                                                 : .File_Name        \ ---                                                                                                           ARCed_Name COUNT TYPE ;                                                                                                     : .File_Sizes       \ ---                                                                                                           sOrig_File 2@ 12 D.R sComp_Data 2@ 12 D.R ;                                                                                 : Show_ARC_Type     \ ---                                                                                                           ARC_Type C@ DUP 4 .R SPACE DUP 4 > OVER 8 < AND SWAP            Max_Type = OR 10 AND 32 + EMIT 2 SPACES ;                                                                                                                                                   \ UNARC - ARCList                                   RS 12/20/87                                                                 : Show_ARC_Data     \ ---       | show info about an ARCed file                                                                     .File_Name 14 ARCed_Name C@ - SPACES Show_ARC_Type              .File_Date 3 SPACES .File_Time .File_Sizes ;                                                                                : ARCList           \ ---       | list the files in an archive                                                                      Get_ARC_Name Open_Input ?SYSERR                                 CR List_Header                                                  BEGIN  Read_ARC_Hdr -1 <>                                       WHILE  CR Show_ARC_Data                                                Skip_File                                                REPEAT Close_Input CR CR ;                                                                                                  \ UNARC - Expand file                               RS 12/20/87                                                                 : Expand_File       \ ---       | expand an archived file                                                                           ARCed_Name Out_File PARSE Create_Output                         IF   CR ARC_Type C@ 7 >                                              IF   ." UnCrunching "     .File_Name UnCrunch_File              ELSE ARC_Type C@ 4 =                                                 IF   ." UnSqeezing " .File_Name UnHUF_File                      ELSE ." UnPacking "  .File_Name UnPack_File                     THEN                                                       THEN Close_Output                                          ELSE Skip_File                                                  THEN ;                                                                                                                                                                                      \ UNARC - UNARC                                     RS 12/20/87                                                                 : UNARC             \ ---       | extract files from an archive                                                                     Get_ARC_Name Open_Input ?SYSERR                                 BEGIN  Read_ARC_Hdr DUP -1 <>                                   WHILE  DUP 7 > SWAP Max_Type < AND                                     IF   Expand_File                                                ELSE CR ." Unable to extract " .File_Name                            ." , file was archived using type "                             ARC_Type C@ . ." compression"                                   Skip_File                                                  THEN                                                     REPEAT DROP Close_Input CR CR ;                                                                                                                                                             \ UNARC                                             RS 12/20/87                                                                 \   ARCList and UNARC will prompt for the name of an ARC file.  \                                                               \   ARCList will list the names, sizes, etc of all entries      \   in the ARC file.  Files marked with an asterisk '*', in     \   the 'Type column cannot be extracted by UNARC.              \                                                               \   UNARC will extract all files from an ARC file except those  \   of types 5, 6 & 7.  If the destination file already         \   exists, you will be asked to verify that it is ok to        \   overwrite the existing file.                                \                                                               \                                                               \                                                                                                                               